# nb_crypto_random (2026-11-08): port of tests/nb_crypto_random_test.sh (shell) to pal + case data (the owner allows no new .sh; AGENTS.md). Drives ONE page through nb_js_worker with the nb_probe op, no window. The probe is a DATA file (&.widgits/_shared-lib/harness/fixtures/nb_probes/rng.js); a new probe is a new .js plus its expected lines.
# ANCHORING: the console capture echoes the probe's own SOURCE, so every token is anchored to a line start with a leading newline (the echo begins with '>'); an unanchored token would match the echo and report a pass or a failure the run did not have.
# NEEDS the real worker binary (ops/+x/nb_js_worker.+x). That binary needs wasm3 to build, which is not in the repo (audit 2026-11-08 P1-5): on a stale binary this case FAILS loudly, which is the truth.
RESULTS | ../results/nb_crypto_random.txt
ENV     | LC_ALL | C
# Two SEPARATE worker processes must draw different random bytes (the bug was a fixed seed: a single-process test cannot see it), and the UUID must be a v4. Collision odds for two 8-byte draws are 2^-64: a failure means not random.
CASE    | crypto-random
SCRATCH |
COPY    | &.hq-apps/network/ops/+x/nb_probe.+x | np.+x
INCLUDE | ../fixtures/nb_page.pdl
COPY    | &.widgits/_shared-lib/harness/fixtures/nb_probes/rng.js | probe.js
RUN | $T/np.+x | --worker | $HOUSE/&.hq-apps/network/ops/+x/nb_js_worker.+x | --page | $T/page.js | --dom | $T/dom.txt | --href | https://example.invalid/ | --title | rng:fixture | --probe | $T/probe.js | --console | $T/console.a.txt | --load-timeout | 30 | --eval-timeout | 30
EXPECT_EXIT | 0 | run-a-completed
RUN | /usr/bin/sed | -n | s/^=>RANDRESULT //p | $T/console.a.txt
CAPTURE | A
RUN | $T/np.+x | --worker | $HOUSE/&.hq-apps/network/ops/+x/nb_js_worker.+x | --page | $T/page.js | --dom | $T/dom.txt | --href | https://example.invalid/ | --title | rng:fixture | --probe | $T/probe.js | --console | $T/console.b.txt | --load-timeout | 30 | --eval-timeout | 30
EXPECT_EXIT | 0 | run-b-completed
RUN | /usr/bin/sed | -n | s/^=>RANDRESULT //p | $T/console.b.txt
CAPTURE | B
EXPECT_NE | $A | $B | two-separate-worker-processes-drew-DIFFERENT-randoms
EXPECT_LACKS | console.a.txt | \n=>RANDRESULT THROW | getRandomValues-did-not-throw
RUN | /usr/bin/grep | -Eq | ^=>RANDRESULT [0-9a-f]{16} [0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-4[0-9a-f]{3}-[89ab][0-9a-f]{3}-[0-9a-f]{12}$ | $T/console.a.txt
EXPECT_EXIT | 0 | 8-lowercase-hex-bytes-then-a-v4-UUID-version-nibble-4-variant-8-9-a-b
CLEAN   |
